      "problem": "$$\n\n$\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})=$",
      "worked_solution": "The definition of $\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡x$ is \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}+\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})}^{2}+1}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}+\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2}+1}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}+\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{2}}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}+\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{6}}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
